MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_001: Yes, Bonaventure? If you have come with military\ncounsel, this may not be the place.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_002: Alas, I have come to discuss my other duties.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_003: Your duty as the keeper of Saramis's history\nand wisdom?
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_004: We of Saramis and the forest peoples have abided\nby a particular rule since the days of Damascar.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_005: As Yu Phas commanded us, we have eschewed\nwriting and maintained a strict oral tradition.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_006: However, the sages are concerned that fragments of\nthis tradition are always being lost.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_007: Including matters related to Yu Phas?
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_008: Those things are still spread widely, but even they\ncannot be maintained forever.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_009: Many of the folk songs retelling the history of the\nland have already been lost to us.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_010: This is a vexing state of affairs. What do you view\nas the cause?
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_011: Fewer and fewer can accurately recite the knowledge\nthat has been passed down.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_012: Even when a mural is preserved, interpretations of\nthe associated story can vary greatly.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_013: Furthermore, human memory is frail. Sometimes\nwhat we remember is not quite what we learned.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_014: I see no remedy for the problem without resorting\nto written records.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_015: That won't do. To adopt writing goes against the\nclear teachings of Yu Phas.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_016: But the lack of it hampers our ability to pass down\nknowledge accurately.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_017: I have not yet found anyone worthy of inheriting\nthe storehouse of my mind. I fear the worst.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_018: Our existence—our future—depends on you finding\na successor. The oral tradition must be maintained.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_019: That will do nothing to prevent the memory of\nSaramis, let alone Damascar, from being lost.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_020: It is a stopgap at best. We ourselves are putting the\ntorch to our kingdom's deeds and works.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_021: I do not wish for our kingdom to slip quietly into the\ndarkness of history. But my hands are tied.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_022: Your Majesty. History is a gift we give to all of the\nchildren who will succeed us.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_023: By the time your future heir realizes we have no\nmeans to convey our history, it will be too late.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_024: My future heir? So we return to that subject, do we?\nEnough, Bonaventure. You are dismissed.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_025: Your Majesty!
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_C_026: As you wish. We shall table this for another time.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_001: Your Majesty, I suggest that you address the troops\nbefore our next battle.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_002: I had the same idea. I am aware that hearing from\nthe queen can benefit morale.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_003: I am pleased to hear it. There is a power in words,\nsurpassing even that of the sword.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_004: Mm. I have heard that my father's words to his\nsoldiers were particularly stirring.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_005: Indeed. No matter how dire the circumstances,\nthey would rally any warrior who heard them.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_006: Regale me, Bonaventure. For surely you know all his\nspeeches by heart.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_007: Very well. This one was delivered in a military\ncampaign in the sixth year of King Sergio's reign.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_008: "Hear me, my proud elite. Horrible brutes have..."
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_009: "Horrible brutes have..."
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_010: What is the matter? Pray continue.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_011: Ah! "Have disgraced Yu Phas, defiled our lands,\nand laid waste to our people."
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_012: "Yu Phas, be with us as we work to undo these\nvile acts!"
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_013: Yes...I can easily see such a speech rousing the\nsoldiers' fervor.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_014: Though it is unlike you to stumble over Father's\nwords so.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_015: I beg your forgiveness, Your Majesty! It is the\nshame of a lifetime.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_016: Peace, Bonaventure. What has come over you?
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_017: It pains me to admit this...
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_018: I feel the sharpness of my mind dulling as the years\npass. I am forgetting things.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_019: Unbelievable...
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_020: You? Keeper of all the knowledge of Saramis,\ncapable of reciting it from memory?
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_021: There is no slowing the march of age. One day I may\neven forget Your Majesty.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_022: Do not say such things. That will never happen.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_023: *sob*
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_024: I beg your pardon. I must take my leave.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_025: Bonaventure...
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_026: Both Father and I relied heavily upon you.
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_027: If not you, who will be there for the future monarch\nof Saramis?
MID_SE_Seo_Bon_B_028: Hnng...
